<edge source="&quot;VENOUS CATHETERIZATION&quot;" target="&quot;SUBENDOCARDIAL INFARCTION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Venous catheterization is likely performed in the context of treating the subendocardial infarction."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ed4025798a84b701fca6f5fd1e1780dd</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;VENOUS CATHETERIZATION&quot;" target="&quot;PULMONARY ARTERY WEDGE MONITORING&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Venous catheterization is a procedure that facilitates the placement of monitors for pulmonary artery wedge pressure."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ed4025798a84b701fca6f5fd1e1780dd</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONGESTIVE HEART FAILURE&quot;" target="&quot;CARDIAC ARREST&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Congestive heart failure is a condition that increases risk of or is related to cardiac arrest events."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ed4025798a84b701fca6f5fd1e1780dd</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONGESTIVE HEART FAILURE&quot;" target="&quot;ACUTE KIDNEY FAILURE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Congestive heart failure is often a contributing factor or comorbid condition with acute kidney failure in a clinical setting."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ed4025798a84b701fca6f5fd1e1780dd</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;OTHER ELECTRIC COUNTERSHOCK OF HEART&quot;" target="&quot;CARDIAC ARREST&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Other electric countershock of heart is a therapeutic intervention administered to correct arrhythmias or restore heart function post-arrest."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ed4025798a84b701fca6f5fd1e1780dd</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTINUOUS INVASIVE MECHANICAL VENTILATION&quot;" target="&quot;CARDIAC ARREST&quot;">
  <data key="d4">14.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Continuous invasive mechanical ventilation is a life support measure associated with the recovery from or risk of cardiac arrest."&lt;SEP&gt;"Continuous mechanical ventilation is often a response to or condition associated with cardiac arrest or shock."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ed4025798a84b701fca6f5fd1e1780dd</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTINUOUS INVASIVE MECHANICAL VENTILATION&quot;" target="&quot;INSERTION OF ENDOTRACHEAL TUBE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Insertion of an endotracheal tube is typically the precursor to or part of invasive mechanical ventilation support."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ed4025798a84b701fca6f5fd1e1780dd</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INSERTION OF ENDOTRACHEAL TUBE&quot;" target="&quot;CARDIAC ARREST&quot;">
  <data key="d4">16.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Insertion of an endotracheal tube is a critical intervention often performed during cardiac arrest events."&lt;SEP&gt;"Insertion of endotracheal tube is a procedure potentially associated with resuscitation from cardiac arrest."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ed4025798a84b701fca6f5fd1e1780dd</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBENDOCARDIAL INFARCTION&quot;" target="&quot;CARDIAC ARREST&quot;">
  <data key="d4">16.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Subendocardial infarction is a coronary artery condition that can lead to or be associated with cardiac arrest."&lt;SEP&gt;"Subendocardial infarction is a significant myocardial injury that can precipitate cardiac arrest."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ed4025798a84b701fca6f5fd1e1780dd</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ACUTE KIDNEY FAILURE&quot;" target="&quot;OTHER SHOCK WITHOUT MENTION OF TRAUMA&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Shock is a physiological state that can lead to acute kidney failure due to hypoperfusion."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ed4025798a84b701fca6f5fd1e1780dd</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UNSPECIFIED SEPTICEMIA&quot;" target="&quot;CELLULITIS AND ABSCESS OF LEG&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Cellulitis and abscess of leg can be a source leading to septicemia in the patient."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ed4025798a84b701fca6f5fd1e1780dd</data>
</edge>
